## Findings
1. blocking — brief:84 This opus adds a background read on visible mount, every 30 s, on window focus and on visibility change, and it reuses `refreshInbox`'s failure branch, which runs `setData(EMPTY)` plus `setReadFailed(true)`. So a single failed background read wipes the queue the Patron is working. That happens when the Patron restarts `bisellium serve` after a pull with the console tab open, or the tab regains focus after sleep before localhost answers. The selection clamps to 0, DOM focus and scroll are lost, and the screen shows the read-failure state. On the next successful read, `currentId` is undefined and `expandedIdRef` is still set, so narrow detail reopens on the first (oldest) petitio instead of the one being read. On master the only read is at mount, and b6 proves only a successful refresh, so no test catches this. Replacement for brief:84: append "A failed refresh after the first successful load keeps the last response, selected id, open detail, DOM focus, scroll and drafts, and shows only the read-failure notice; only a failed first load renders the empty read-failure state. Served b6 aborts one interval `/api/inbox` read and asserts all of these are retained." [severity: S1] [design: keeps] [class: spec×promise-unattainable-under-accepted-domain] — check: none: a served W-407-b6 row that fails one background `/api/inbox` read at 1280 and 390 with detail open and a half-typed ratio, then asserts the queue, `aria-selected`, detail subject, active element and ratio are unchanged after the failure and after recovery
2. advisory — brief:60 "The response may retain its pre-existing studio field" is false. Master's `needsYou()` returns `{ opera, petitiones }`, and the prototype adds `studio: this.studioDir`. Since revision f no Inbox Colophon reads it, so the field is dead output that exposes the absolute studio path. brief:39, brief:40 and brief:51 still list it as a seam. Replacement for brief:60's last sentence: "The response adds no studio field; `InboxResponse` gains only `opened?`." Drop "and studio" from brief:39 and brief:51, and change brief:40 to "the one backward-compatible response field". [severity: S2] [class: spec×prose-contradiction-under-revision] — check: none: a server test asserting `needsYou()`'s keys are exactly `opera, petitiones`
3. advisory — brief:21 This line says 1.21:1 wash on surface "passes both named AA criteria". That is true only of the two criteria it names. When the wash is the only selected/focus indicator, WCAG 1.4.11 Non-text Contrast (3:1 for state indicators) is not met. This is the Patron's ruling (revision f: no underline or box), so it makes sense as an accepted trade-off. It should not read as AA conformance. Replacement for brief:21's sentence: "…2.4.11 is met because the row is unobscured; 1.4.11's 3:1 for a state indicator is not met at 1.21:1, a trade-off the Patron accepted in revision f (no underline/box/outline)." Apply the same to brief:169. [severity: S2] [class: spec×prose-contradiction-under-revision] — check: none
4. advisory — brief:102 On tab return, `focus` and `visibilitychange` both fire, so every return issues two overlapping `/api/inbox` reads. A stale read that resolves after the post-answer read takes whichever `refreshIntentRef` it finds. The limits name "overlapping resolution order", so this is stated. A one-line coalescing guard (skip while a read is in flight) would make it moot. Replacement: append "a return to the tab issues two reads; their order is a limit" to brief:102. [severity: S3] [class: tests×ruled-case-uncovered] — check: none

## Verdict
The input boundary stays sound: strict `instant()`, the stable comparator, the guarded read-set codec and the ID-keyed drafts all hold. The Patron-ruled Outlook layout and the wash-only selection make sense on the approved captures. But the new background refresh wipes and misplaces the Patron's decision on any failed read, which breaks brief:84. The fix keeps the design and goes to the build as a required fix.
VERDICT: FAIL
